          "line_end": 72,
          "line_start": 69,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L69-L72"
        },
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 560,
          "line_start": 556,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L556-L560"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_7da57c1829709a1b39fe015293f554ad6434126071b10c08155465b6f4019eff",
        "slc_cea58e5559d114d62479aafeff68f2ca71c8f8da62b24c4378a5b32c688609c7"
      ],
      "text": "Documentation describes an explicit agent lifecycle moving through Uninitialized, Initializing, Running, Stopping and Stopped, with any state able to transition to an Error state on failure."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_c6ce283c6a9311c402be2b9cb45ac246f41dd74cdc812a280afec3a3379c0e1d",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "tools-permissions",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 282,
          "line_start": 279,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L279-L282"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_348da6accbaf1dc7a6355198b028f0af22cbacf778f1b68361b4de2418737931"
      ],
      "text": "Listed tool-execution security controls include JSON-schema validation of parameters, per-tool process isolation with timeouts, and restricting available tools to an allow-list."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_fd4cc04f0f0c6bb196ea2241262581ce69d2ab73c38155a2b3c5358e65a098cc",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "dependencies",
      "kind": "observation",
