          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L862-L862"
        },
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 870,
          "line_start": 866,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L866-L870"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_b5fab2ab7164fa6053521e91686fe96c3b214fe5cdb74d2f267b01e939fe2c33",
        "slc_ebf73b01453257cda1e9a9c02ca550c87379501899672a0dbd4ad793e4ac6e35"
      ],
      "text": "An accepted architecture decision record states Rust was chosen for the core implementation, citing memory safety without garbage-collection overhead and strong async support as rationale."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_3b5d917c455185f35669ddd1720db8f4053dd56edb676bc092c72b28dd78233c",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "dependencies",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 885,
          "line_start": 885,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L885-L885"
        },
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 899,
          "line_start": 896,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L896-L899"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_6634ad9c195870d5dcbf02f36b5a35143cbfaf530400631360a3b9103f7c7b34",
        "slc_ea59de757e7095964b68157cfeeb3ddb8ef480761a05adf8607ffd62eafda91d"
      ],
      "text": "A second accepted decision record names rumqttc as the MQTT client library, noting it avoids external C dependencies since it is a pure-Rust implementation."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_0e8319ee1c7a4658b65ec1218313a80514e3998cfe89b389333076ef4236cc57",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "limitations",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 877,
          "line_start": 874,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L874-L877"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_628bdba193e7f2f83cf80637f2543b017a749762859d779c691befdcaef5588d"
      ],
      "text": "The Rust-language decision record acknowledges two consequences: a steeper learning curve for contributors unfamiliar with Rust, and longer compile times than an interpreted language would have."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_08094b898032f30087693c9da28d6e638d9bf0c3792e2890bfbcce87657dcba4",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "tools-permissions",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689",
          "git_sha": "2e1183b0c22a986e165b2760f0640b2ba20a5956",
          "line_end": 629,
          "line_start": 626,
          "path": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
          "repository": "2389-research/2389-agent-rust",
          "url": "https://github.com/2389-research/2389-agent-rust/blob/9ebe8438dbdb0a9566ef9ce4d6f492fc253db689/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L626-L629"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_86f84c2c8fde23fc69c06a965bdd256a3055c9ad167feef0b41169ba17f41298"
      ],
      "text": "The threat model names four trust boundaries: the MQTT network perimeter, process isolation around tool execution, the LLM provider API boundary, and input validation at the data boundary."
    }
